{
  "name": "Cworth CE-H6K / CE-LBW-48100C (PACE BMS)",
  "description": "Wired Modbus-RTU profile for Cworth CE-H6K / CE-LBW-48100C PACE BMS. Unit ID 1 and little-endian byte order are inferred from the existing wired profile template; confirm both against hardware before use. Pack current polarity is preserved as reported: negative=charge, positive=discharge. Wiring: battery COMM port pin 7 = RS485-A-PCS and pin 8 = RS485-B-PCS; connect ONLY these two pins. Hazard: pin 3 carries +5V; do NOT connect pin 3 to a USB-RS485 adapter or use a straight-through 8-pin cable. Only one pack can be reliably polled per physical RS485 bus: packs default to Modbus address 0 and there is no documented way to set a unique address over the wire. Inverter setup: set Program 01 to LIb (lithium) and connect the comms cable BEFORE power-cycling the inverter, because the BMS handshake occurs only at boot.",
  "protocol": "modbus-rtu",
  "transport": "rs232",
  "default_unit_id": 1,
  "byte_order": "le",
  "defaults": {
    "baud": 9600,
    "dataBits": 8,
    "stopBits": 1,
    "parity": "none"
  },
  "metrics": [
